{"findings":[{"rule_id":"NM-002","evidence":[{"kind":"title_block","ref":"material","page":1,"quote":"Polyurethene"},{"kind":"note","ref":"N2","page":1,"quote":"SHORE HARDNESS- 80±5"},{"kind":"title_block","ref":"heat_treatment","page":1,"quote":"HARDENED 40-45 HRC"}],"comment":"The title block specifies the material as 'Polyurethene' and note N2 gives a Shore hardness of '80±5', yet the heat treatment field states 'HARDENED 40-45 HRC'. Rockwell C hardness is a metallic scale that cannot be applied to polyurethane, creating a direct contradiction that will confuse manufacturing. The designer should remove or correct the heat treatment field to match the polymer material."

  ,
  "recommended_correction": "Remove the 'HARDENED 40-45 HRC' heat treatment entry from the title block, as it contradicts the polyurethane material and the Shore hardness specified in note N2."}]}
